WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
A map of a forest.

2
00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:04.900
A lookout tower stands on each side of it.

3
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.950
Smoke rises somewhere among the trees.

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.950
Neither lookout can
tell how far away it is.

5
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.560
Each one can read just a
compass bearing to the smoke.

6
00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:20.310
So how can a map and a protractor
turn two bearings into one exact spot?

7
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.330
In this mission, you'll
measure three-figure bearings,

8
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.750
turning clockwise from north,
like oh six five degrees.

9
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.960
You'll draw a bearing line from
a point on a scale drawing,

10
00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.230
where one centimetre
represents one kilometre.

11
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.970
And you'll measure a
distance on the drawing,

12
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.500
then convert it with the scale.

13
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:43.810
Your mission: explain how two bearings
from two lookouts pinpoint the fire.
